From 26b7c9654df3aa1a1bc0e9dcb0950cb7952356cc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ththeod <2376818+ththeod@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 17:00:34 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 099/138] RAM KV tier with RecoverSSM: native CPU offloading
 for the hybrid model

- Allow the native CPU OffloadingConnector together with RecoverSSM
  (VLLM_E2_RECOVERSSM_OFFLOAD=1); P/D and every other connector stay rejected.
  VLLM_E2_BOUNDARY_OFFLOAD_HOLD_STEPS / VLLM_E2_MAMBA_HIT_DEFER_STEPS tune when
  boundary states are stored and when a Mamba hit is deferred.
- Uniform worker KV stride for the shared offload region under pipeline
  parallelism (VLLM_OFFLOAD_WORKER_KV_BYTES_PER_BLOCK): the region interleaves
  one slot per worker inside each chunk, and PP ranks holding different layers
  derived different strides, so slots overlapped and reloads were corrupted.
- Register the whole mmap as pinned memory with cudaHostRegister, resetting
  CUDA's sticky error and retrying when registration fails.
- Scratch filtering keeps the scheduler/worker allocation stride.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
